{"name":"Fizzy & Dizzy","hex":"#f7f5c8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fizzy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["(of a liquid) Containing bubbles.","Lively, vivacious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A non-alcoholic carbonated beverage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fizzy"},{"term":"dizzy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Experiencing a sensation of whirling and of being giddy, unbalanced, or lightheaded.","Producing giddiness."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (someone or something) dizzy; to bewilder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dizzy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Effervescence","blocks":[{"text":"Effervescence is the escape of gas from an aqueous solution and the foaming or fizzing that results from that release. The word effervescence is derived from the Latin verb fervere, preceded by the prefix ex. It has the same linguistic root as the word fermentation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Soda_bubbles_macro.jpg/330px-Soda_bubbles_macro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Effervescence"},{"title":"Ampersand","blocks":[{"text":"The ampersand, also known as the and sign, is the logogram &, representing the conjunction \"and\". It originated as a ligature of the word et."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Et_sign.svg/330px-Et_sign.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ampersand"},{"title":"Dizziness","blocks":[{"text":"Dizziness is an imprecise term that can refer to a sense of disorientation in space, vertigo, or lightheadedness. It can also refer to disequilibrium or a non-specific feeling, such as giddiness or foolishness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Depiction_of_a_person_feeling_dizzy.png/330px-Depi